          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "is inherited: CDIAL lists the Hindi cousin thāmnā, \"to prop, to stop\", under Sanskrit stambhate (CDIAL 13683); تھمنا (thamnā) is the form for something that stops by itself, تھمانا the one for handing something over."
            }
